MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The End of Heartache feels like a natural next choice after In Flames and Soilwork because I want heavy riffs paired with melodic choruses.",
    "City of Evil fits my interest in involved guitar work, while The Sickness gives me a reason to explore more Disturbed after Ten Thousand Fists."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "St. Anger's raw, abrasive sound misses the balance of heaviness and melody I want right now, even though it shares the heavy sound of other albums here.",
    "Hybrid Theory's hooks appeal to me, but I am choosing guitar-focused metal today; liking it does not make it my next pick."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in aggressive music seems to have been treated as a broad preference for heaviness, although the melodic side is what makes many of these albums appealing to me.",
    "Albums that connect to some part of my listening seem to be treated as equally timely, even though I would save several of them for another visit."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated interest in In Flames and Soilwork makes the combination of melodic riffs, intensity, and memorable choruses especially relevant to my choices today.",
    "My recent Ten Thousand Fists interaction gives The Sickness a specific appeal: I want to hear more from that artist, beyond simply finding another heavy album."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You understood my interest in heavy music, but my strongest choices depend on melody, guitar work, and what I want to explore next."
}
